---
// About: who makes Elsewhere, how submitting works, where each detail comes from, how sure we are, and what
// the labels and numbers on the site mean. Every figure here is counted from the data, not written by hand.
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Icon from '../components/Icon.astro';
import { places } from '../lib/places';
import { directionsIsSearch } from '../lib/discovery';
import { breadcrumbs, abs } from '../lib/seo';
const visited = places.filter(p => p.visited).length;
const exact = places.filter(p => !directionsIsSearch(p)).length;
const years = places.map(p => Number(p.addedAt.slice(0, 4)));
const [from, to] = [Math.min(...years), Math.max(...years)];
const site = Astro.site!;
const jsonLd = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'AboutPage', '@id': abs('/about/', site), url: abs('/about/', site), name: 'About Elsewhere', inLanguage: 'en-GB',
  isPartOf: { '@id': abs('/#website', site) }, about: { '@id': abs('/#organization', site) }, breadcrumb: breadcrumbs([['Home', '/'], ['About']], site) };
const steps = [
  { icon: 'magnifying-glass', title: 'Find the place', text: 'Start typing its name and pick it from the Google Maps suggestions, so we get the exact spot. You can also just type the name.' },
  { icon: 'wifi-high', title: 'Say what you found', text: 'Yes, no or not sure for Wi-Fi, sockets, laptops, calls and step-free access. Add a speed test, the Wi-Fi password or a note if you have them.' },
  { icon: 'paper-plane-tilt', title: 'Send it', text: 'It’s saved for review straight away, marked Pending. You only see “Thanks, that’s in” once it’s saved. If sending fails, it stays on your device so you can try again.' },
  { icon: 'check-circle', title: 'We check it', text: 'Every report is read by hand. Places that fit are added as Reported; nothing is published automatically.' },
];
const sources = [
  { icon: 'note-pencil', title: 'Tajdid’s list', text: `${places.length} places noted between ${from} and ${to}: Wi-Fi speed, sockets, noise and how to get online. Each detail is dated by when it was added, and a speed is one test from then, not a live reading.` },
  { icon: 'clipboard-text', title: 'Your reports', text: 'What visitors tell us. Reports stay separate from the list until they’re checked; then the detail gets the new date and its source.' },
  { icon: 'map-trifold', title: 'Google Maps', text: `Where a place is: exact directions and a small map for ${exact} places, and opening hours shown live when you tap “Show hours”. Google’s details aren’t copied into the list.` },
];
---
<Layout title="About" seoTitle="About Elsewhere: how places are chosen and checked | Elsewhere" description="Who makes Elsewhere, how submitting a place works, where each detail comes from, and what Reported and Verified mean." jsonLd={jsonLd}>
<article class="about">
 <header class="about-head">
  <h1>About Elsewhere.</h1>
  <p class="lead">A short list of places in Dubai where you can open a laptop and get some work done: cafés, co-working spaces, restaurants and bars. Each place shows what matters before you go: how fast the Wi-Fi is, whether you’ll find a socket, how noisy it gets and how to get online.</p>
  <dl class="about-figures">
   <div><dt>places on the list</dt><dd>{places.length}</dd></div>
   <div><dt>worked from by Elsewhere</dt><dd>{visited}</dd></div>
   <div><dt>with exact directions</dt><dd>{exact}</dd></div>
  </dl>
 </header>

 <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="who">
  <h2 id="who">Who’s behind it</h2>
  <div class="about-body">
   <p>Elsewhere is made by <a href="https://tajdidrahman.co.uk" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Tajdid Rahman<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>. It started as a personal list of places to work from around Dubai, noting the Wi-Fi, the sockets and whether a call would be drowned out. This site turns that list into something anyone can browse, and anyone can add to.</p>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="submitting">
  <h2 id="submitting">How submitting works</h2>
  <div class="about-body">
   <ol class="about-steps">
    {steps.map((s, i) => <li>
     <span class="about-step-top"><span class="about-step-n" aria-hidden="true">{i + 1}</span><Icon name={s.icon} weight="fill" size={20} /></span>
     <h3>{s.title}</h3>
     <p>{s.text}</p>
    </li>)}
   </ol>
   <p class="about-note">Been to a place that’s already listed? Use “Report what you found” on its page; it works the same way.</p>
   <a class="primary about-cta" href="/submit/"><Icon name="plus" weight="bold" size={16} anim="spin" />Submit a place</a>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="sources">
  <h2 id="sources">Where the details come from</h2>
  <div class="about-body">
   <ul class="about-sources">
    {sources.map(s => <li><Icon name={s.icon} weight="fill" size={22} /><h3>{s.title}</h3><p>{s.text}</p></li>)}
   </ul>
   <p class="about-note">When none of these says something, the site shows “not added” instead of guessing.</p>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="labels">
  <h2 id="labels">How sure we are</h2>
  <div class="about-body">
   <p>Each detail on a place page carries its own label. A detail is Verified only when someone has checked it in person and dated it within the last 90 days. Dates are never moved forward without a new check, so an old date means old information. No detail is Verified yet; everything on the site today is Reported.</p>
   <dl class="glossary glossary--pills">
    <div><dt><span class="pill" data-tone="caution">Yes · Reported</span></dt><dd>From our list or a visitor, not rechecked yet.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><span class="pill" data-tone="positive">Yes · Verified</span></dt><dd>Checked in person, with a date, within the last 90 days.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><span class="pill" data-tone="caution">Yes · Needs recheck</span></dt><dd>It was verified, but more than 90 days ago.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><span class="pill" data-tone="caution">Conflicting reports</span></dt><dd>Sources disagree, so nothing is claimed until it’s checked again.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><span class="pill" data-tone="unknown">Not checked</span></dt><dd>No reliable information yet.</dd></div>
   </dl>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="meaning">
  <h2 id="meaning">What things mean</h2>
  <div class="about-body">
   <dl class="glossary">
    <div><dt><Icon name="lightning" size={18} />Wi-Fi speed</dt><dd>Download speed from one speed test, taken when the place was added. 50+ Mbps is plenty for video calls, 20+ is good, 5+ is fine for email and browsing. Speeds change, so older tests say they need a retest.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><Icon name="plug" size={18} />Sockets</dt><dd>How easy it is to plug in, from 1 to 5: A few, Some, Fair, Plenty, Lots.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><Icon name="speaker-high" size={18} />Noise</dt><dd>Quiet: calls are fine. Moderate: some background noise, calls are okay. Loud: best avoided for calls.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><Icon name="lock-simple" size={18} />Wi-Fi access</dt><dd>The guest password when we have it (tap Copy), or how to get on: no password, ask staff, or a sign-up page. Passwords change, so ask staff if one doesn’t work.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><Icon name="check-circle" size={18} />Visited</dt><dd>Someone from Elsewhere has worked from there.</dd></div>
    <div><dt><Icon name="question" size={18} />Not added</dt><dd>We don’t have that detail yet. If you know it, tell us.</dd></div>
   </dl>
  </div>
 </section>

 <section class="about-section" aria-labelledby="small-print">
  <h2 id="small-print">Good to know</h2>
  <div class="about-body">
   <ul class="about-list">
    <li><strong>Photos are stand-ins.</strong> Every place shows a temporary photo, not the venue itself, until we have a real one. Place pages say so on the photo.</li>
    <li><strong>Directions</strong> open Google Maps: straight to the place for {exact} places, otherwise a search by name, so check it’s the right one.</li>
    <li><strong>Hours come from Google Maps</strong> when you ask, and holiday hours can differ. Check with the venue before a long day out, and ask staff about laptops at busy times.</li>
    <li><strong>Saved places stay on this device.</strong> They live in your browser, don’t sync anywhere and need no account. Clearing your browser data removes them.</li>
    <li><strong>Your email is optional.</strong> If you leave one with a report, it’s only used to ask about that report and is never shown on the site.</li>
    <li><strong>Visits are counted without cookies,</strong> using Vercel Web Analytics. There are no accounts and no ads.</li>
   </ul>
  </div>
 </section>
</article>
</Layout>
